    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1cf2210d_ff6db991",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/core/ir/transform/decompose_uniform_access.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 965,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002241
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-20T22:58:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Because we\u0027ve changed the element type of the array, and potentially added more stuff to it. e.g.\n```\nstruct S {\n  a: u32,\n  b: u32,\n  arr: array\u003cvec4\u003cf32, 4\u003e\u003e,\n}\nvar v: S;\n\nBecomes:\nvar v : array\u003cu32\u003e\n```\nThe number of elements in the new array is different, so we need to figure out the length of the original array.",
      "parentUuid": "e4c07ecd_03665ffa",
      "revId": "3be88fc1fe222e2abe101cc8fd2d8fec1eee11ef",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "65392131_b9758d50",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/core/ir/transform/decompose_uniform_access.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 965,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002266
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-20T23:04:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Imagine you have\n```\nstruct S {\n  a : vec4u,\n  b : array\u003cu32\u003e\n}\n@group(0) @binding(0) var\u003cstorage\u003e v : S;\n```\nThe original arrayLength returns the number of elements in S.b and new arrayLength returns that value + 4 (S.a) (assuming u32 base type). So we have to account for the offset to get to the runtime-sized array. Previously that would only be possible with a constant offset (struct member), but bufferView can introduce a runtime offset via it\u0027s operand.",
      "parentUuid": "e4c07ecd_03665ffa",
      "revId": "3be88fc1fe222e2abe101cc8fd2d8fec1eee11ef",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
